<Routines>
<Routine Name="a1_MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided "AS IS" -- No warranty or implied merchantability.
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[=================================================================

Sample program for new Kinematics feature of  5 Axis Delta Kinematics, via MCTO, MCPM programming;
MCTO is programed Target positions are programmed using path positions in the MCPM instruction. 


=====  MCTO Set up  =====
Cartesian system = CS_XYZRxRyRz (6 Virtual axes, Geometry=Cartesian, Definition = XYZRxRyRz)
Robot coordinate system = Delta5D_J1J2J3J4J5 (5 Joint axes, Geometry=Delta 3D, Definition = J1J2J3J4J5)  


================================================================
Open Trend = to view the plot of robot’s TCP Positions 
	XY Plot shows object positions on the conveyor at TCP and End of Arm(EOA)
XZ Plot shows TCP moves during different pick cycles 

==================================================================
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[JSR(VectorDynamics,0) ,JSR(a2_Delta5D_PICK_PLACE,0) ,JSR(a3_JogMaster,0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[==========================
USER SETUP:::
Toggle bits from left to right.
===========================
Select Type of MCPM move. Refer readme_file routine for more details on different types of MCPM moves.  
 Initiate_MCTO: Enables the Transformation between the Cartesian axes and Robot axes
Start_PickPlace: Does a PICK and PLACE with a speed invariant path.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(MCPM_Incremental_Move) ,XIC(MCPM_Absolute_Move) ,XIC(MCPM_RzMove_Coupling) ,XIC(MCPM_with_WorkTool) ]XIC(Initiate_MCTO)XIC(Start_PickPlace)OTU(unlatch);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stop the Program]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCSCart)XIC(MCSRobot)OTU(Stop_Program);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="a2_Delta5D_PICK_PLACE" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(s:fs)XIC(Robot.GroupSynced)MOV(-2,step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Home the Joint axes before initiating MCTO]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Robot.GroupSynced)EQU(step,-2)MAH(J1_v,Mah_Ctr[0])MAH(J2_v,Mah_Ctr[1])MAH(J3_v,Mah_Ctr[2])MAH(J4_v,Mah_Ctr[3])MAH(J5_v,Mah_Ctr[4])XIC(Mah_Ctr[0].DN)XIC(Mah_Ctr[1].DN)XIC(Mah_Ctr[2].DN)XIC(Mah_Ctr[3].DN)XIC(Mah_Ctr[4].DN)MOV(-1,step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,-1)[XIC(MCPM_Incremental_Move) COP(Delta5D_Inc_Path[0],Delta5D_Path[0],10) ,XIC(MCPM_Absolute_Move) COP(Delta5D_Abs_Path[0],Delta5D_Path[0],10) ,XIC(MCPM_RzMove_Coupling) COP(Codian_Abs_Rz_Path[0],Delta5D_Path[0],10) ,XIC(MCPM_with_WorkTool) COP(Delta5D_Work_Tool_Path[0],Delta5D_Path[0],10) COP(MCPM_WorkFrame,workframe,1) COP(MCPM_ToolFrame,toolframe,1) ]MOV(1,step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Enable MCTO followed by Motion Coordinated Master Driven Speed Control for controlling the speed of the PICK PLACE through single virtual master]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Initiate_MCTO)XIC(Robot.GroupSynced)EQU(step,1)[MCTO(CS_XYZRxRyRz,Delta5D_J1J2J3J4J5,mcto1,workframe,toolframe) XIC(mcto1.IP) MDCC(CS_XYZRxRyRz,VirtualMaster,mdcc1,Command,1.0) ,XIC(mdcc1.IP) MOV(2,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============PICK AND PLACE Moves ================]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_PickPlace)EQU(step,2)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm[0],Delta5D_Path[0],1,dyn_data,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(mcpm[0].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(3,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,3)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm[1],Delta5D_Path[1],1,dyn_data,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(mcpm[1].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(4,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,4)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm[2],Delta5D_Path[2],1,dyn_data,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(mcpm[2].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(5,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,5)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm[3],Delta5D_Path[3],1,dyn_data,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(mcpm[3].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(6,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,6)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm[4],Delta5D_Path[4],1,dyn_data,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(mcpm[4].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(7,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,7)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm[5],Delta5D_Path[5],1,dyn_data,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(mcpm[5].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(8,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,8)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm[6],Delta5D_Path[6],1,dyn_data,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(mcpm[6].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(9,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,9)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm[7],Delta5D_Path[7],1,dyn_data,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(mcpm[7].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(10,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,10)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm[8],Delta5D_Path[8],1,dyn_data,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(mcpm[8].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(3,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCSCart)MCS(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcs1,Coordinated Transform,0,0,0,0,0,0)OTU(MCSCart);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCSRobot)MCS(Delta5D_J1J2J3J4J5,mcs2,Coordinated Transform,0,0,0,0,0,0)OTU(MCSRobot);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="a3_JogMaster" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(maj1.EN)MAJ(VirtualMaster,maj1,0,majMaster,0,50,0,50,0,0,10,10,0,0,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="readme_file" Type="ST">
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[(*]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[ /*  ============================================================================= */	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[				  DELTA 5 Axis Robot with Orientation Control   ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[ /*  ============================================================================= */	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[This program contains a 5-Axis Delta Robot demonstrating a simple PICK and PLACE in XYZ plane with Ry andRz orientation control.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[It also demonstrates the Speed override functionality (scaling the entire PICK and PLACE dynamics using a single master axis).]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[a2_Delta5D_PICK_PLACE routine overview: ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[1. MCTO links the Cartesian XYZRxRyRz and Delta-4Axis Robot Coordinate systems (Coordinate Definition for Delta 4 Axis is J1J2J3J6) and transforms the motion]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[2. MDCC is the master driven speed control instruction that links the Cartesian coordinate system to the virtual master axis for speed override functionality.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[3. Using MCPM Path move instruction, the Robot is programmed to move to a known Absolute Start Position. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[4. Rest of the pick and place moves are programed different ways]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="16">
<![CDATA[	a.	Incremental moves with Ry and Rz orientations  ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="17">
<![CDATA[	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="18">
<![CDATA[	Incremental moves are programed with 100 Up (AB) followed by 400 horizontal (BC) and 100 down (CD)in XZ plane, last 100 (DE) on DE plane.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="19">
<![CDATA[	The same is repeated in the reverse direction for the PLACE move in YZ plane.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="20">
<![CDATA[	Along with the Cartesian moves, the Path moves are also programmed with Rz orientation. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="21">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="22">
<![CDATA[					 __________________________  ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="23">
<![CDATA[				  B |            400           | C]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="24">
<![CDATA[				100 |                          |  ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="25">
<![CDATA[					|                          |100]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="26">
<![CDATA[					|                          |      100 ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="27">
<![CDATA[				  A |                        D |__ __ __ __ E ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="28">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="29">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="30">
<![CDATA[	 The Ry and Rz Orientation moves are programmed incremental along with the primary cartesian axes as below:]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="31">
<![CDATA[		AB =   Ry\@ 0  degrees and Rx\@ 0    degrees]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="32">
<![CDATA[		BC =   Ry\@-45 degrees and Rx\@ 765  degrees]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="33">
<![CDATA[		CD =   Ry\@-45 degrees and Rx\@ 45   degrees]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="34">
<![CDATA[		DE =   Ry\@ 0  degrees and Rx\@ 0    degrees]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="35">
<![CDATA[		ED =   Ry\@ 0  degrees and Rx\@ 0    degrees]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="36">
<![CDATA[		DC =   Ry\@ 45 degrees and Rx\@ -45  degrees]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="37">
<![CDATA[		CB =   Ry\@ 45 degrees and Rx\@ -765 degrees]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="38">
<![CDATA[		BA =   Ry\@ 0  degrees and Rx\@ 0    degrees ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="39">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="40">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="41">
<![CDATA[	b.	Absolute moves with Ry and Rz orientations  ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="42">
<![CDATA[		]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="43">
<![CDATA[		Same A,B,C,D,E  Positions  shown are programmed using absolute positions. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="44">
<![CDATA[		Refer Delta5D_Abs_Path[].Position[] array for absolute position values. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="45">
<![CDATA[		Turns counter feature on J4 axis is used here for Rz moves. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="46">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="47">
<![CDATA[	c.	Absolute moves with only Rz orientations.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="48">
<![CDATA[	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="49">
<![CDATA[		These moves will show specific “ J4:J5 coupling ration”feature of 5 axis Delta geometries. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="50">
<![CDATA[		When  you move only Rz axis it will move J4 and J5 axis to remove the coupling effect by J4 axis. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="51">
<![CDATA[		Rz positions are programmed using multiple turns with “Turns counter “feature. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="52">
<![CDATA[		Refer Delta5D_Abs_Rz_Path[].Position[] array for absolute position values. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="53">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="54">
<![CDATA[	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="55">
<![CDATA[	d.	Incremental move with Work and Tool frame offsets. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="56">
<![CDATA[	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="57">
<![CDATA[		These moves will show Work frame feature on 5 axis delta robots.  ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="58">
<![CDATA[		Work frame is transferred to End Of Arm of robot using work frame offset values. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="59">
<![CDATA[		Sometimes this will helps user to program target end position from EOA. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="60">
<![CDATA[		Work Frame offsets =  X= 27.5, Y = 0, Z = -781.968, Rx = 0 ,Ry = 0, Rz =0, Refer MCPM_WorkFrame parameter for Work frame offset values. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="61">
<![CDATA[		Refer Delta5D_Work_Tool_Path[].Position array for incremental end positions. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="62">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="63">
<![CDATA[6. The command tolerance for the first move is set to 100 units and the second move is set to 50  units for the PICK cycle.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="64">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="65">
<![CDATA[7. The dynamics of the path move are all programmed in % of max (dyn_data.UnitsMode  is set to 0). ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="66">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="67">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="68">
<![CDATA[a3_JogMaster routine overview:]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="69">
<![CDATA[1.	Jogging the VirtualMaster axis using MAJ instruction will provide the speed override functionality for the PICK and PLACE cycle.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="70">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="71">
<![CDATA[VectorDynamics. MainRoutine Overview:]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="72">
<![CDATA[1. The routine calculates the Cartesian Vector velocity and the Orientation vector velocity.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="73">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="74">
<![CDATA[See online help 'Configure the Delta J1J2J3J4J5 Coordinate System' for more information on configuring Delta 5 axis Delta robots. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="75">
<![CDATA[See  online help 'Blending Path Moves with MCPM for more information on the PICK and PLACE Cycle']]>
</Line>
<Line Number="76">
<![CDATA[*)]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="77">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="VectorDynamics" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Vector velocity of Cartesian Coordinate System]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(VectorVelocity,SQR(X.ActualVelocity**2 + Y.ActualVelocity**2+Z.ActualVelocity**2));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Vector Acceleration of the cartesian Cooridnate system]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(VectorAcceleration,SQR(X.CommandAcceleration**2+Y.CommandAcceleration**2+Z.CommandAcceleration**2));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
<Program Name="VectorDynamics" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="eventTask" Disabled="false">
<Tags/>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="eventTask" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(OrtVectorVelocity,SQR( Rx.ActualVelocity**2 + Ry.ActualVelocity**2+ Rz.ActualVelocity**2))CPT(CartVectorVelocity,SQR(X.ActualVelocity**2 + Y.ActualVelocity**2+Z.ActualVelocity**2));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
